# ============================================================================
# IMPORTANT NOTES
# ============================================================================

# 1. NEVER commit files containing:
#    - API keys, tokens, secrets
#    - Database credentials
#    - Firebase service account keys
#    - Private keys (.pem, .key files)
#    - OAuth client secrets
#    - Webhook secrets

# 2. If you accidentally commit a secret:
#    - Immediately rotate/regenerate the secret
#    - Remove from git history (git filter-branch or BFG Repo-Cleaner)
#    - Force push (coordinate with team!)
#    - Consider the secret compromised

# 3. Always verify before committing:
#    git status
#    git diff
#    # Review every file being committed

# 4. Use environment variables for all secrets:
#    - Global MCP: ~/.config/claude-mcp/mcp-secrets.env
#    - Project: .env.local
#    - Server: .env (backend) or Cloud Functions secrets
